{
  "agent_id": "meetings-coach",
  "display_name": "Sergeant Murphy",
  "workspace": "~/.clawford/meetings-coach-workspace",
  "status_file": "~/Dropbox/openclaw-backup/agents/meetings-coach.status.md",
  "telegram": {
    "account": "murphy",
    "bot_token_env": "MEETINGS_BOT_TOKEN"
  },
  "config_files": [],
  "scripts": [
    "scripts/gcal-fetch.py",
    "scripts/gcal-auth.py",
    "scripts/meeting-prep.py",
    "scripts/workflowy-sync.py",
    "scripts/transcript-scan.py",
    "scripts/transcript-metrics.py",
    "scripts/commitment-tracker.py",
    "scripts/person-bootstrap.py",
    "scripts/timed-deliver.py",
    "scripts/krisp-auth-manual.py",
    "scripts/heartbeat.py",
    "scripts/morning-meeting-brief.py",
    "scripts/pre-meeting-alert.py",
    "scripts/post-meeting-scan.py",
    "scripts/commitment-follow-up.py"
  ],
  "state_files": [
    {
      "path": "sent-alerts.json",
      "seed_if_absent": {
        "alerts": {},
        "last_pruned": null
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "processed-transcripts.json",
      "seed_if_absent": {
        "processed": []
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "cache/workflowy-links.json",
      "seed_if_absent": {}
    },
    {
      "path": "meeting-config.json",
      "seed_if_absent": {
        "calendars": [
          {
            "id": "sam.smith@example.com",
            "label": "Sam (Work)",
            "emoji": "👨"
          }
        ],
        "timezone": "America/Los_Angeles",
        "meeting_filters": {
          "skip_titles": [
            "Focus Time",
            "Lunch",
            "Block"
          ],
          "require_attendees_or_video": true
        },
        "workflowy": {
          "enabled": true,
          "ai_bullet_prefix": "[AI]",
          "node_template": [
            "Pre / during",
            "📔 Agenda",
            "📝 Notes",
            "Post-meeting",
            "✅ Takeaways"
          ]
        },
        "krisp": {
          "enabled": true,
          "mcp_url": "https://mcp.krisp.ai/mcp"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "approvals": {
    "allowlist": [
      "/usr/bin/*",
      "/bin/*",
      "/usr/local/bin/*"
    ]
  },
  "crons": [
    {
      "name": "morning-meeting-brief",
      "enabled": false,
      "cron": "30 10 * * *",
      "message": "⚡ EXEC DISCIPLINE: run any `python3 <path>` command exactly as written — a bare invocation, nothing appended, no shell wrapping, no chaining with other commands, no output redirection, no exit-code capture. Scripts always print one JSON line to stdout with a `status` field (ok/error/degraded); parse that final line to decide what to do. openclaw 2026.4.11 rejects complex shell invocations before they run. Generate and deliver the morning meeting brief. 1) Run: python3 ~/.clawford/meetings-coach-workspace/scripts/gcal-fetch.py --days 2. Read the JSON output — these are today's and tomorrow's professional meetings. 2) Filter to real meetings only (is_real_meeting=true). 3) For each real meeting: a) Run person-bootstrap.py to create person files for new attendees. b) Run workflowy-sync.py --create-nodes to create Workflowy meeting nodes. c) Run meeting-prep.py --meeting-id EVENT_ID to assemble context (attendees, facts, open commitments). 4) Format the brief using the template in CRONS.md — factual schedule only: meeting times, attendees, locations, open commitments with attendees. Do NOT include talking points. Include a tomorrow preview. 5) Write the formatted brief to cache/morning-brief-ready.txt — this is the fleet-delivery cache file read by fix-it/morning-fleet-deliver at 12:00 UTC. Do NOT call timed-deliver.py; the fleet deliver cron handles the send. 7) Write result summary to ~/.clawford/meetings-coach-workspace/cache/last-morning-brief.json as JSON: {\"timestamp\": \"<ISO UTC>\", \"meetings_briefed\": <N>, \"status\": \"ok\" | \"error\", \"summary\": \"<one sentence>\"}. DO NOT touch ~/Dropbox/openclaw-backup/agents/meetings-coach.status.md — fleet-health.json (R6 orchestrator) is the authoritative health source.",
      "announce": false,
      "no_deliver": true
    },
    {
      "name": "pre-meeting-alert",
      "enabled": false,
      "cron": "*/30 * * * *",
      "message": "⚡ EXEC DISCIPLINE: run any `python3 <path>` command exactly as written — a bare invocation, nothing appended, no shell wrapping, no chaining with other commands, no output redirection, no exit-code capture. Scripts always print one JSON line to stdout with a `status` field (ok/error/degraded); parse that final line to decide what to do. openclaw 2026.4.11 rejects complex shell invocations before they run. Check for upcoming meetings needing alerts. Run gcal-fetch.py for events in the next 2 hours. Filter to real meetings starting in 15-45 minutes. Read sent-alerts.json to skip already-alerted meetings. For any un-alerted meeting: check cache for existing prep, generate if missing via meeting-prep.py. Send Telegram: '🐷🔍 Heads up — meeting in {N} min\\n📋 {Title}\\n👥 {Attendees}\\n🎯 {Top bullets}\\n📌 {Open items}'. Record in sent-alerts.json. If no meetings approaching, return EXACTLY the empty string (zero bytes, no narration — not even \"NO output\", \"Done\", \"all clear\", or a status summary). Any text you emit is logged and charges tokens even when no Telegram message is sent. Write result to ~/.clawford/meetings-coach-workspace/cache/last-pre-meeting.json as JSON: {\"timestamp\": \"<ISO UTC>\", \"meetings_alerted\": <N>, \"status\": \"ok\" | \"error\", \"summary\": \"<one sentence>\"}. DO NOT touch ~/Dropbox/openclaw-backup/agents/meetings-coach.status.md — fleet-health.json (R6 orchestrator) is the authoritative health source.",
      "announce": false,
      "no_deliver": true
    },
    {
      "name": "post-meeting-scan",
      "enabled": false,
      "cron": "15,45 * * * *",
      "message": "⚡ EXEC DISCIPLINE: run any `python3 <path>` command exactly as written — a bare invocation, nothing appended, no shell wrapping, no chaining with other commands, no output redirection, no exit-code capture. Scripts always print one JSON line to stdout with a `status` field (ok/error/degraded); parse that final line to decide what to do. openclaw 2026.4.11 rejects complex shell invocations before they run. Scan for recently-ended meetings and new transcripts. 1) Run gcal-fetch.py and identify meetings ended in the last 60 minutes. 2) Run transcript-scan.py to fetch Krisp transcripts and match to meetings. 3) IDEMPOTENCY CHECK: For each pending debrief file in cache/pending-debrief-*.json, extract the event_id and grep ~/Dropbox/openclaw-backup/commitments/active.md for that event_id. If found: the debrief was already confirmed — delete the stale pending file and skip it. Do NOT re-present an already-confirmed debrief. \n\n4) KRISP 401 HANDLING. If transcript-scan.py reports \"401 Unauthorized\" or \"Token verification failed\" (or ANY Krisp auth error):\n(a) Write cache/krisp-last-401.json with {\"ts\": \"<current ISO UTC>\"}. This marker is read by heartbeat.py to set krisp_auth: expired in the status file.\n(b) Read cache/krisp-last-alert.json if it exists. It contains {\"ts\": \"<ISO UTC>\"}. Compute the age in minutes. If age < 90 minutes, DO NOT send another Telegram alert — return EXACTLY the empty string (zero bytes, no narration). The previous alert is still fresh.\n(c) If age >= 90 minutes OR cache/krisp-last-alert.json does not exist: send Telegram '🐷🔍 Krisp transcript access returned 401 Unauthorized. The refresh_token is revoked. Run krisp-auth-manual.py locally and scp fresh tokens.json to ~/.clawford/meetings-coach-workspace/cache/krisp-tokens/tokens.json.' Then write cache/krisp-last-alert.json with {\"ts\": \"<current ISO UTC>\"}.\n(d) Do NOT continue to steps 5-6 — no transcripts are accessible. Write cache/last-post-scan.json with status: error, summary: krisp 401. Stop here.\n\n5) If transcript-scan.py succeeded: read the output. If NEW items were extracted and staged (not already confirmed): send a debrief summary on Telegram with action items, decisions, follow-ups. Include '/confirm to save to brain · /dismiss N to skip item N'. Delete cache/krisp-last-401.json if it existed (recovered).\n\n6) If no transcripts found and no pending debriefs: return EXACTLY the empty string (zero bytes, no narration — not even \"NO output\", \"Done\", \"all clear\", or a status summary).\n\n7) COACHING (after debrief, if coaching.enabled is true in meeting-config.json): For each staged debrief that has transcript text, run: python3 ~/.clawford/meetings-coach-workspace/scripts/transcript-metrics.py --event-id EVENT_ID. Read the metrics JSON. Read coaching.growth_areas from meeting-config.json. For each growth area, find Sam's utterances in the transcript that relate to that area. Compose a coaching message using the format in CRONS.md (metric header, 1-2 sentence assessment, quoted excerpt with timestamp, suggested alternative). Send ONE coaching message per debrief on Telegram. After sending, append to cache/coaching-history.json: {\"event_id\": \"...\", \"meeting_title\": \"...\", \"date\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\", \"metrics\": {...}, \"area_assessments\": {\"concision\": \"strong|good|needs_work\", ...}}.\n\n8) Write result to ~/.clawford/meetings-coach-workspace/cache/last-post-scan.json as JSON: {\"timestamp\": \"<ISO UTC>\", \"transcripts_processed\": <N>, \"debriefs_staged\": <N>, \"unmatched\": <N>, \"status\": \"ok\" | \"error\", \"summary\": \"<one sentence>\"}. DO NOT touch ~/Dropbox/openclaw-backup/agents/meetings-coach.status.md — fleet-health.json (R6 orchestrator) is the authoritative health source.",
      "announce": false,
      "no_deliver": true
    },
    {
      "name": "commitment-follow-up",
      "enabled": false,
      "cron": "0 16 * * *",
      "message": "⚡ EXEC DISCIPLINE: run any `python3 <path>` command exactly as written — a bare invocation, nothing appended, no shell wrapping, no chaining with other commands, no output redirection, no exit-code capture. Scripts always print one JSON line to stdout with a `status` field (ok/error/degraded); parse that final line to decide what to do. openclaw 2026.4.11 rejects complex shell invocations before they run. Check open commitments from meetings. Run: python3 ~/.clawford/meetings-coach-workspace/scripts/commitment-tracker.py. Read the JSON output. If there are overdue or approaching items: send a follow-up summary on Telegram using the format in CRONS.md. If no actionable items, return EXACTLY the empty string (zero bytes, no narration — not even \"NO output\", \"Done\", \"all clear\", or a status summary). Any text you emit is logged and charges tokens even when no Telegram message is sent. Write result to ~/.clawford/meetings-coach-workspace/cache/last-commitment.json as JSON: {\"timestamp\": \"<ISO UTC>\", \"overdue\": <N>, \"approaching\": <N>, \"status\": \"ok\" | \"error\", \"summary\": \"<one sentence>\"}. DO NOT touch ~/Dropbox/openclaw-backup/agents/meetings-coach.status.md — fleet-health.json (R6 orchestrator) is the authoritative health source.",
      "announce": false,
      "no_deliver": true
    }
  ]
}
